{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Client Hints Image Negotiation.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Client Hints Image Negotiation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"client hints image negotiation client hints image negotiation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Client Hints Image Negotiation.md","fileName":"Client Hints Image Negotiation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Client Hints Image Negotiation","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-28 04:01\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Adaptive Image Delivery and Caching]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Adaptive Image Delivery and Caching","Accept-CH Opt-In","Vary Header for Image Variants","highperformanceimages.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Client Hints Image Negotiation.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Client Hints Image Negotiation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"client hints image negotiation client hints image negotiation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Client Hints Image Negotiation.md","fileName":"Client Hints Image Negotiation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Client Hints Image Negotiation","heading":"Client Hints Image Negotiation","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Client hints move some responsive-image context from HTML into HTTP request headers. After the server opts in, a client can describe properties such as viewport width, device pixel ratio, requested resource width, network capacity, or a preference to save data.\n\nThe server uses those inputs to choose or generate a suitable representation and must identify the request dimensions that affect the response. This separates presentation markup from delivery logic, but increases caching and privacy complexity. See [[Accept-CH Opt-In]] and [[Vary Header for Image Variants]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Adaptive Image Deliv